<title>PORTUGAL: FORECAST - Portugal spreads vs Bunds/Bonos.</title>
<headline>FORECAST - Portugal spreads vs Bunds/Bonos.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1997-06-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following is the daily forecast for spreads in the Portuguese bond market based on a poll of four banks and a dealer.</p>
<p>Poll covers spreads between the February 2007 Portuguese cash bond (OT) and the German and Spanish equivalents, together with the spreads between the Portuguese 10 and two-year bonds.</p>
<p>--------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>			     Min spread Avge  Max  vs previous close</p>
<p>Feb 07 vs Bund July  07   67 bps   68.4  70	    68</p>
<p>Feb 07 vs Bono March 07    -7    -8.2   -10	    -8</p>
<p>				 Min  Avge   Max</p>
<p>Feb 07 vs March 99	 119  121.6  125     vs     121</p>
<p>----------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>Key factors likely to affect market:</p>
<p>- Ten-year Portuguese bonds will remain glued to comments on the euro and eagerly await U.S. jobs data, dealers said.</p>
<p>----------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>--Sergio Goncalves, Lisbon bureau 3511-3150035</p>
</text>
